<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Alarcos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1195">1195</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Alarcos · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Alarcos was fought in 1195 in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaqub-al-mansur">Abu Yusuf Yaqub al-Mansur</a> and King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-viii">Alfonso VIII</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>. The Almohads won a major victory. It marked the high point of Almohad power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, although it was reversed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-navas-de-tolosa">Las Navas de Tolosa</a> in 1212.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-alarcos.jpg" alt="Battle of Alarcos" width="256" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ciudad_Real,_Spain_location.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The caliphate mounted the last great Muslim offensive against Christian Iberia, and the <b>Battle of Alarcos</b> (1195) showed that a unified Muslim power could still threaten the advance of the Christian kingdoms.</blockquote><a href="/empire/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Alfonso VIII took Cuenca in 1177 but was crushed by the Almohads at the <b>Battle of Alarcos</b> in 1195.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Kingdom of Castile · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Their leader Mahyu fought for the Almohad victory at the <b>Battle of Alarcos</b> in 1195 and died of his wounds; his son Abd al-Haqq, born in the Zab to a noble family, was the effective founder of the dynasty.</blockquote><a href="/empire/marinid-sultanate">Marinid Sultanate · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
